  "intro": "Bryce Canyon is not really a canyon at all but a chain of giant natural amphitheaters cut into the eastern edge of the Paunsaugunt Plateau. Frost and running water have carved its soft pink and orange rock into thousands of thin spires called hoodoos. The park sits much higher than nearby Zion, with a rim between 8,000 and 9,000 feet.",
