  "facts": [
   "It is named for Ebenezer Bryce, a Mormon settler who grazed cattle here and reputedly called it a \"helluva place to lose a cow.\"",
   "Bryce Amphitheater, the largest of the park's amphitheaters, is 12 miles long, 3 miles wide and 800 feet deep.",
   "Some hoodoos stand up to 200 feet tall; the oranges come from hematite, the yellows from limonite and the purples from pyrolusite.",
   "The night sky is so dark that visitors can see about 7,500 stars, and it became an International Dark Sky Park in 2019.",
   "The park holds the largest protected population of the threatened Utah prairie dog, which was reintroduced there."
